hite, then he's kind. But we don't know if Bob is white. So we can't conclude from rule 17.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 18 again. If Bob is rough and kind, he's smart. But we don't know if Bob is kind. However, from rule 16, if someone is kind, they're young. Bob is young, so if he's kind, he's smart. But we don't know if he's kind.\n\nAlternatively, from rule 15, smart things are cold. So if Bob is smart, he's cold. But from rule 20, all smart, cold things are kind. So if Bob is smart, he's cold and thus kind. But we don't know if Bob is kind.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 18 again. If Bob is rough and kind, he's smart. But we don't know if Bob is kind. However, from rule 16, if someone is kind, they're young. Bob is young, so if he's kind, he's smart. But we don't know if he's kind.\n\nAlternatively, from rule 17, white things are kind. If Bob is white, then he's kind. But we don't know if Bob is white.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 18 again. If Bob is rough and kind, he's smart. But we don't know if Bob is kind. However, from rule 16, if someone is kind, they're young. Bob is young, so if he's kind, he's smart. But we don't know if he's kind.\n\nAlternatively, from rule 15, smart things are cold. So if Bob is smart, he's cold. But from rule 20, all smart, cold things are kind. So if Bob is smart, he's cold and thus kind. But we don't know if Bob is kind.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 18 again. If Bob is rough and kind, he's smart. But we don't know if Bob is kind. However, from rule 16, if someone is kind, they're young. Bob is young, so if he's kind, he's smart. But we don't know if he's kind.\n\nAlternatively, from rule 17, white things are kind. If Bob is white, then he's kind. But we don't know if Bob is white.\n\nWait, but let's think about rule 18 again. If Bob is rough and kind, he's smart. But we don't know if Bob is kind. However, from rule 16, if someone is kind, they're young. Bob is young, so if he's kind, he's smart. But we 